  "id": "medical-model",
  "term": "medical model",
  "definition": "In this context, the medical model is a way of understanding distress through a syndrome-based, illness-focused lens that treats painful thoughts and emotions as symptoms to be corrected or reduced. It can frame moral suffering as pathology rather than as a human moral response.",
